==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|en|Fredericston}} {{q|historical spelling}}

===Etymology===
From {{m|en|Fredericston}}, from {{af|en|Frederic|-s-|-ton}}. The city was named after {{w|lang=en|Prince Frederick, Duke of York and Albany}} (1763 - 1827) by colonial governor {{w|lang=en|Thomas Carleton}}.

